  "title": "Regular -ER and -IR verbs in the present tense",
  "unit": "A1",
  "group": "Grammar",
  "order": 12,
  "summary": "Comer, beber, aprender, vivir, escribir: two families with almost the same endings.",
  "focus": "Present indicative of regular -er and -ir verbs",
  "prerequisites": [
    "a1-regular-ar-present"
  ],
  "content": "## The other two families\n\nAfter **-ar**, the remaining verbs end in **-er** (*comer*, *beber*, *aprender*, *leer*) or **-ir** (*vivir*, *escribir*, *abrir*). The pattern is the same as for -ar verbs: remove the ending, add the person ending.\n\n## The endings\n\n| person | -er: comer | -ir: vivir |\n|---|---|---|\n| yo | com**o** | viv**o** |\n| tú | com**es** | viv**es** |\n| él / ella / usted | com**e** | viv**e** |\n| nosotros/as | com**emos** | viv**imos** |\n| vosotros/as | com**éis** | viv**ís** |\n| ellos / ellas / ustedes | com**en** | viv**en** |\n\nThe two families differ only in the **nosotros** and **vosotros** forms: *comemos / vivimos*, *coméis / vivís*. Everywhere else, -er and -ir verbs are identical.\n\n## More examples\n\n- *Aprendo español.* (I'm learning Spanish.)\n- *¿Bebes café?* (Do you drink coffee?)\n- *Vivimos en Sevilla.* (We live in Seville.)\n- *Mis hermanos escriben mucho.* (My brothers write a lot.)\n- *¿Dónde vive usted?* (Where do you live?)\n\n*Leer* (to read) is regular in the present: *leo, lees, lee, leemos, leéis, leen*.\n\n## Spot the accent\n\nAs with *-áis*, the vosotros endings carry an accent: **-éis** and **-ís**. No other form does.",
